WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.667 --> 00:00:01.835
-President Trump

00:00:01.835 --> 00:00:03.737
and senior members
of the Republican Party

00:00:03.737 --> 00:00:06.673
are engaged in an assault
on democracy,

00:00:06.673 --> 00:00:08.974
in an attempt to hang on
to power and undercut

00:00:08.974 --> 00:00:11.877
the legitimately elected
next president, Joe Biden,

00:00:11.877 --> 00:00:14.614
and they put Rudy Giuliani
in charge of their plan.

00:00:14.614 --> 00:00:17.083
For more on this,
it's time for "A Closer Look."

00:00:17.083 --> 00:00:21.187
♪♪

00:00:21.187 --> 00:00:24.224
Look, it's very unlikely
this dumbass coup attempt

00:00:24.224 --> 00:00:27.560
by Trump and his gang
of weirdo, lopsided goons,

00:00:27.560 --> 00:00:28.728 line:0%
or, as I'm calling them...

00:00:30.763 --> 00:00:32.999 line:0%
...will succeed,
but it's alarming enough

00:00:32.999 --> 00:00:34.266
that they're trying.

00:00:34.266 --> 00:00:35.702
And we are finding out,
right now,

00:00:35.702 --> 00:00:37.804
who, in the Republican Party,
would be willing to go along

00:00:37.804 --> 00:00:39.906
with an actual coup attempt
in the future

00:00:39.906 --> 00:00:41.440
if, say, an election
was much closer

00:00:41.440 --> 00:00:44.143
or if they had another chance
to accept criminal interference

00:00:44.143 --> 00:00:46.712
from a foreign country,
or if Rudy Giuliani tried

00:00:46.712 --> 00:00:49.515
to break into a ballot machine
to change votes for Trump,

00:00:49.515 --> 00:00:51.383
only to realize
it's a pinball machine

00:00:51.383 --> 00:00:52.885
at a pizzeria in Yonkers.

00:00:52.885 --> 00:00:53.986
[ As Giuliani ]
Boss, great news.

00:00:53.986 --> 00:00:57.123
I got you 500 more votes
and an extra ball!

00:00:57.123 --> 00:00:58.791
You've got
the secretary of State joking

00:00:58.791 --> 00:00:59.859
about a possible coup,

00:00:59.859 --> 00:01:01.360
the White House press secretary

00:01:01.360 --> 00:01:03.429
insisting Trump will
remain president,

00:01:03.429 --> 00:01:05.965
and prominent Fox hosts
straight-up demanding

00:01:05.965 --> 00:01:07.667
that Republicans refuse
to accept

00:01:07.667 --> 00:01:09.101
the results of the election.

00:01:09.101 --> 00:01:11.003
-Is the State Department
currently preparing

00:01:11.003 --> 00:01:13.072
to engage with the
Biden transition team

00:01:13.072 --> 00:01:15.074
and, if not,
at what point does a delay

00:01:15.074 --> 00:01:16.876
hamper a smooth transition

00:01:16.876 --> 00:01:20.046
or pose a risk
to national security?

00:01:20.046 --> 00:01:22.148
-There will be
a smooth transition

00:01:22.148 --> 00:01:23.716
to a second
Trump administration.

00:01:23.716 --> 00:01:25.885 line:0%
-He's left an infrastructure
in place

00:01:25.885 --> 00:01:27.754 line:0%
where COVID
can be handled

00:01:27.754 --> 00:01:30.189 line:0%
and we believe that we will do
so going forward

00:01:30.189 --> 00:01:31.758 line:0%
in a second
Trump administration.

00:01:31.758 --> 00:01:32.992 line:0%
-Yeah, please.
-What I'd like to know is

00:01:32.992 --> 00:01:35.394 line:0%
what in the hell is
the Republican Party doing

00:01:35.394 --> 00:01:39.365 line:0%
to defend and to --
I mean, why not just say

00:01:39.365 --> 00:01:41.767 line:0%
"We're not going to accept
the results of this election"?

00:01:41.767 --> 00:01:43.002
-I don't know.
Why not just say,

00:01:43.002 --> 00:01:45.238
"Lou Dobbs should get
a head reduction surgery"

00:01:45.238 --> 00:01:47.307
or "Lou Dobbs looks
like a child at a wedding

00:01:47.307 --> 00:01:48.641
after a million bee stings"

00:01:48.641 --> 00:01:50.643
or "How does
this 75-year-old man

00:01:50.643 --> 00:01:53.279
have hair the same color
as a brand-new penny"?

00:01:53.279 --> 00:01:54.614
They're not magic words.

00:01:54.614 --> 00:01:56.582
It doesn't matter
whether you say them or not.

00:01:56.582 --> 00:01:58.251
You can't go to a doctor's
appointment,

00:01:58.251 --> 00:02:01.220
get an X-ray that shows you have
a spoon stuck in your esophagus

00:02:01.220 --> 00:02:02.822
because you didn't realize

00:02:02.822 --> 00:02:04.357
it wasn't part of the meal
and then say...

00:02:04.357 --> 00:02:07.526
[ As Dobbs ]
I refuse to accept
the results of this X-ray.

00:02:07.526 --> 00:02:09.862
Second, you're lighting
American democracy on fire,

00:02:09.862 --> 00:02:11.030
you fascist Bobblehead.

00:02:11.030 --> 00:02:12.832
The vast majority of Americans

00:02:12.832 --> 00:02:14.234
accept the outcome
of the election

00:02:14.234 --> 00:02:16.269
and the reality
that it was free and fair,

00:02:16.269 --> 00:02:18.471
but Republicans
who listen to your [bleep]

00:02:18.471 --> 00:02:20.573
are starting to echo
your deranged rhetoric

00:02:20.573 --> 00:02:21.574
about how it was rigged.

00:02:21.574 --> 00:02:22.842
A poll out today

00:02:22.842 --> 00:02:24.711
found that about half
of Republicans

00:02:24.711 --> 00:02:27.079
think Trump won the election
and it was rigged against him.

00:02:27.079 --> 00:02:29.716
And, look, the people
who show up to Trump rallies,

00:02:29.716 --> 00:02:30.749
you could probably get them

00:02:30.749 --> 00:02:32.918
to agree with anything
Trump says.

00:02:32.918 --> 00:02:36.022
If you're willing to give up
your day to stand in a field

00:02:36.022 --> 00:02:37.857
and listen to third-rate
stand-up comedy

00:02:37.857 --> 00:02:42.428
from a man who loathes you,
you're what they call pliable.

00:02:42.428 --> 00:02:43.696
Now, as we told you
earlier this week,

00:02:43.696 --> 00:02:44.997
there are some
Republican officials

00:02:44.997 --> 00:02:46.966
who have met
the absolute lowest bar,

00:02:46.966 --> 00:02:49.635
by acknowledging that Joe Biden
is the president-elect

00:02:49.635 --> 00:02:51.371
and should be treated as such.

00:02:51.371 --> 00:02:53.406
Arkansas Governor Asa Hutchinson
said...

00:02:56.309 --> 00:02:58.044
And Ohio Governor Mike DeWine
said...

00:03:00.212 --> 00:03:02.648
Tells you just how sick
our political culture is,

00:03:02.648 --> 00:03:05.918
that a Republican official
just acknowledging the obvious

00:03:05.918 --> 00:03:08.021
and legitimate winner
of a presidential election

00:03:08.021 --> 00:03:10.757
is somehow considered
a brave, noteworthy act.

00:03:10.757 --> 00:03:12.525
It's like picking up
your morning newspaper

00:03:12.525 --> 00:03:13.660
and the headline says...

00:03:17.763 --> 00:03:20.466
And, yet, aside from those
rare exceptions,

00:03:20.466 --> 00:03:23.702
many Republican politicians
remain in lockstep behind Trump

00:03:23.702 --> 00:03:25.905
as he continues to pretend
he has a path

00:03:25.905 --> 00:03:28.941
to overturn the election results
that declare victory.

00:03:28.941 --> 00:03:30.944
Texas Lieutenant Governor
Dan Patrick,

00:03:30.944 --> 00:03:32.745
the same guy who said, in March,

00:03:32.745 --> 00:03:34.847
that old people should be
willing to die from COVID

00:03:34.847 --> 00:03:37.082
to keep the economy
from shutting down,

00:03:37.082 --> 00:03:40.920
spelled out Trump's supposed
path to victory on Fox News.

00:03:40.920 --> 00:03:43.155 line:0%
-There's less
than 30,000 votes,

00:03:43.155 --> 00:03:45.958 line:0%
in Georgia and Arizona,

00:03:45.958 --> 00:03:48.728 line:0%
dividing Biden
and Trump.

00:03:48.728 --> 00:03:51.230 line:0%
And, if those two states turn,
if they do,

00:03:51.230 --> 00:03:52.731 line:0%
then the Supreme Court
could make the decision

00:03:52.731 --> 00:03:55.201 line:0%
on Pennsylvania,
and then Trump is president.

00:03:55.201 --> 00:03:58.070
-The last plan I heard with that
many insane contingencies

00:03:58.070 --> 00:04:01.173
is my cousin explaining how he's
going to pay back that loan.

00:04:01.173 --> 00:04:04.811
[ Stoner voice ]
If the lady I dogsit for
puts me in her will

00:04:04.811 --> 00:04:06.679
and then, she dies

00:04:06.679 --> 00:04:09.682
and then, it goes uncontested
by her kids,

00:04:09.682 --> 00:04:11.951
I'm going to have your money.

00:04:11.951 --> 00:04:14.086
By the way, Dan Patrick
is also the dude

00:04:14.086 --> 00:04:16.021 line:0%
who offered a reward
of $1 million

00:04:16.021 --> 00:04:17.991 line:0%
for evidence of voter fraud
in Texas,

00:04:17.991 --> 00:04:20.526 line:0%
which, I have to say,
kind of disproves

00:04:20.526 --> 00:04:21.961 line:0%
the point you're trying to make.

00:04:21.961 --> 00:04:25.664 line:0%
If voter fraud is so common that
it could overturn an election,

00:04:25.664 --> 00:04:28.334 line:0%
why do you need to offer
a million-dollar reward

00:04:28.334 --> 00:04:29.635 line:0%
to find some evidence of it?

00:04:29.635 --> 00:04:30.937 line:0%
In the Old West, when they

00:04:30.937 --> 00:04:32.738
offered rewards for outlaws,

00:04:32.738 --> 00:04:34.540
it was because they
were hard to find.

00:04:34.540 --> 00:04:35.842
They weren't just squatting

00:04:35.842 --> 00:04:37.543
behind a barrel
in the town square.

00:04:37.543 --> 00:04:40.245
"Hey, uh, I think that's
Billy the Kid over there.

00:04:40.245 --> 00:04:43.116
Can I have my --
can I have my million now?"

00:04:43.116 --> 00:04:45.017
But, anyway, that's
their harebrained scheme.

00:04:45.017 --> 00:04:47.253
They want to somehow
flip Arizona and Georgia,

00:04:47.253 --> 00:04:48.988
then go to court
to get Pennsylvania

00:04:48.988 --> 00:04:50.723
to throw out,
not just a few ballots,

00:04:50.723 --> 00:04:52.592
but hundreds of thousands
of ballots,

00:04:52.592 --> 00:04:54.927
and have the Supreme Court
hand the election to Trump.

00:04:54.927 --> 00:04:56.895
And, apparently, in Georgia,

00:04:56.895 --> 00:04:59.132
the guy who's leading the effort
to overturn the results

00:04:59.132 --> 00:05:00.465
is Congressman Doug Collins.

00:05:00.465 --> 00:05:03.135
The Georgia secretary of State,
Brad Raffensperger,

00:05:03.135 --> 00:05:04.570
who's a Republican,

00:05:04.570 --> 00:05:08.006
went so far as to call Collins
a liar and a charlatan.

00:05:08.006 --> 00:05:09.275
Now, you might remember Collins

00:05:09.275 --> 00:05:12.312
as the insanely
fast-talking person

00:05:12.312 --> 00:05:13.912
who took a lead role
for Republicans

00:05:13.912 --> 00:05:15.314
during the impeachment
proceedings.

00:05:15.314 --> 00:05:16.782 line:0%
-We've talked about the law.
The law wasn't broken.

00:05:16.782 --> 00:05:17.983 line:0%
They didn't put it
in the Constitution,

00:05:17.983 --> 00:05:19.385 line:0%
so I can yell on both of them.

00:05:19.385 --> 00:05:20.619 line:0%
I can talk about both of them.

00:05:20.619 --> 00:05:22.088 line:0%
I still have
not got a transcript.

00:05:22.088 --> 00:05:24.023 line:0%
We still don't know what --
And the White House

00:05:24.023 --> 00:05:25.157 line:0%
still has not got their stuff.

00:05:25.157 --> 00:05:26.191 line:0%
I was told I couldn't.

00:05:26.191 --> 00:05:27.193 line:0%
Even though there had been

00:05:27.193 --> 00:05:28.727 line:0%
staff conversations well before,

00:05:28.727 --> 00:05:31.263 line:0%
I was told I was asking
too late.

00:05:31.263 --> 00:05:33.633 line:0%
He said, "Can you," as he said,
"help us, as a country,

00:05:33.633 --> 00:05:35.234 line:0%
because we're
trying to heal."

00:05:35.234 --> 00:05:36.703
-He sounds like
he's auctioning off

00:05:36.703 --> 00:05:39.438
the cocaine from a drug bust
after taking the test himself.

00:05:39.438 --> 00:05:41.173
[ As Collins ]
We got one kilo, we have
two kilos, we have five kilos.

00:05:41.173 --> 00:05:42.574
We got gold-plated guns,
we got regular guns,

00:05:42.574 --> 00:05:44.109
we got tiny, little guns.

00:05:44.109 --> 00:05:45.911
Then, there's South Carolina
Senator Lindsey Graham,

00:05:45.911 --> 00:05:48.514
who, according to Raffensperger,
who, again, is a Republican,

00:05:48.514 --> 00:05:51.850
called and pressured him
to throw out legal ballots.

00:05:51.850 --> 00:05:54.420 line:0%
-Georgia's secretary of State
Brad Raffensperger,

00:05:54.420 --> 00:05:57.189 line:0%
says he's come under increasing
pressure in recent days

00:05:57.189 --> 00:06:00.726 line:0%
from Republicans intent
on questioning the validity

00:06:00.726 --> 00:06:03.762 line:0%
of legally cast
absentee ballots,

00:06:03.762 --> 00:06:05.398 line:0%
in an effort
to reverse

00:06:05.398 --> 00:06:08.467 line:0%
President Trump's loss
in the state.

00:06:08.467 --> 00:06:10.002 line:0%
In an interview
with The Washington Post,

00:06:10.002 --> 00:06:12.137 line:0%
Raffensperger said
Senator Lindsey Graham

00:06:12.137 --> 00:06:13.272 line:0%
asked him on Friday

00:06:13.272 --> 00:06:15.407 line:0%
if he had the power
to toss out ballots

00:06:15.407 --> 00:06:20.146 line:0%
in counties found to have higher
rates of nonmatching signatures.

00:06:20.146 --> 00:06:22.581 line:0%
Raffensperger said
he was stunned

00:06:22.581 --> 00:06:24.016 line:0%
that Graham appeared to suggest

00:06:24.016 --> 00:06:28.187 line:0%
that he find a way to toss
legally cast ballots.

00:06:28.187 --> 00:06:29.455
-So Lindsey Graham called up

00:06:29.455 --> 00:06:30.923
the secretary of State
of Georgia,

00:06:30.923 --> 00:06:32.992
like it was a casual schmooze,
and said,

00:06:32.992 --> 00:06:34.293
"Hey, Brad, want to do brunch?

00:06:34.293 --> 00:06:36.662
Also, do you have the power
to like throw out

00:06:36.662 --> 00:06:38.898
a bunch of legal ballots
and hand the election to Trump?"

00:06:38.898 --> 00:06:40.766
Now, according
to The Wall Street Journal,

00:06:40.766 --> 00:06:43.335
there were two phone calls
and multiple witnesses

00:06:43.335 --> 00:06:45.972
who confirmed what Graham said
on those calls.

00:06:45.972 --> 00:06:47.672
And, even when Graham
tried denying it,

00:06:47.672 --> 00:06:48.707
he accidentally confessed

00:06:48.707 --> 00:06:51.377
to something
possibly even worse --

00:06:51.377 --> 00:06:54.380
that he'd been calling election
officials in other states, too.

00:06:56.982 --> 00:06:58.450 line:0%
-No.
That's ridiculous.

00:06:58.450 --> 00:07:00.820 line:0%
I talked to him about how
you verify signatures.

00:07:00.820 --> 00:07:03.221 line:0%
I'm really worried
about mail-in balloting,

00:07:03.221 --> 00:07:05.357 line:0%
I'm worried about how
you verify a signature,

00:07:05.357 --> 00:07:07.059 line:0%
and I think Georgia --

00:07:07.059 --> 00:07:09.562 line:0%
I've talked to Doug Ducey
in Arizona.

00:07:09.562 --> 00:07:11.463 line:0%
I've talked to the
people in Nevada.

00:07:11.463 --> 00:07:13.732 line:0%
We've got contests all
over the nation.

00:07:13.732 --> 00:07:15.100
-So, basically, Lindsey Graham

00:07:15.100 --> 00:07:16.568
called states
where Joe Biden won

00:07:16.568 --> 00:07:17.970
to ask about vote counts.

00:07:17.970 --> 00:07:20.205
I'd say they were threatening
calls, but it's impossible

00:07:20.205 --> 00:07:21.907
for Lindsey Graham
to sound threatening.

00:07:21.907 --> 00:07:25.044
He has the voice of a guy
offering to redo your veranda.

00:07:25.044 --> 00:07:26.546
[ As Graham ]
I, for one, can't enjoy

00:07:26.546 --> 00:07:29.782
an iced tea on my porch swing
if I'm looking at chipped paint.

00:07:29.782 --> 00:07:31.450
This is the trademark
Trump defense.

00:07:31.450 --> 00:07:33.585
Their only explanation
for their bad behavior

00:07:33.585 --> 00:07:35.454
is more bad behavior.

00:07:35.454 --> 00:07:37.723
Graham's like an arsonist
defending himself in court

00:07:37.723 --> 00:07:39.492
by saying, "What about all those
other houses I burned down?

00:07:39.492 --> 00:07:40.860
You didn't seem
to care about that.

00:07:40.860 --> 00:07:43.496
Maybe you're the ones who need
to look in the mirror!"

00:07:43.496 --> 00:07:46.165
And, Lindsey, we might take
your word at face value --

00:07:46.165 --> 00:07:48.601
and I mean might --
if you hadn't promised

00:07:48.601 --> 00:07:51.203
to never support the appointment
of a Supreme Court justice

00:07:51.203 --> 00:07:53.072
in an election year
and then, this year,

00:07:53.072 --> 00:07:54.206
when that was put to the test

00:07:54.206 --> 00:07:56.308
with Amy Coney Barrett,
told reporters --

00:07:56.308 --> 00:07:59.178
[ As Graham ]
I said a fib before,
but, now, I ain't fibbin'.

00:07:59.178 --> 00:08:01.947
Now, I'm saying
my for real thoughts.

00:08:01.947 --> 00:08:04.016
So that was their attempt
to steal Georgia

00:08:04.016 --> 00:08:05.551
and they fell flat
on their faces.

00:08:05.551 --> 00:08:07.153
Then, there's Pennsylvania,

00:08:07.153 --> 00:08:09.321
where the Trump campaign
is suing for --

00:08:09.321 --> 00:08:11.323
I don't know, reasons?

00:08:11.323 --> 00:08:13.592
It's impossible to keep
track of their bull[bleep]

00:08:13.592 --> 00:08:15.127
It's like your mom
and dad trying

00:08:15.127 --> 00:08:16.862
to tell you a story
at the same time.

00:08:16.862 --> 00:08:18.163
"So, we're at Chili's, right?"

00:08:18.163 --> 00:08:19.398
It was an Applebee's.

00:08:19.398 --> 00:08:21.033
"No, Applebee's was Tuesday.

00:08:21.033 --> 00:08:23.402
I'm talking about the waiter
who dropped the tray."

00:08:23.402 --> 00:08:24.736
That was an Applebee's!

00:08:24.736 --> 00:08:26.438
For example,
they're all worked up

00:08:26.438 --> 00:08:29.074
over an electronic voting
system called Dominion

00:08:29.074 --> 00:08:31.644
because there was a small
and brief reporting mistake

00:08:31.644 --> 00:08:33.279
on election night in Michigan.

00:08:33.279 --> 00:08:34.646
But even the conservative,
pro-Trump

00:08:34.646 --> 00:08:37.383
Wall Street Journal
editorial board pointed out...

00:08:55.834 --> 00:08:57.670
A Republican county clerk
even said...

00:09:01.440 --> 00:09:04.176
And, if anyone should understand
human error, it's Trump.

00:09:04.176 --> 00:09:06.045
I mean, he is a human error.

00:09:06.045 --> 00:09:07.880
The guy couldn't pronounce
the word Yosemite,

00:09:07.880 --> 00:09:09.715
he couldn't figure out how
to close an umbrella,

00:09:09.715 --> 00:09:12.351
and couldn't even get the toilet
paper off his shoe after,

00:09:12.351 --> 00:09:15.787
I guess, taking a giant dump
inside the presidential limo?

00:09:15.787 --> 00:09:17.623
I mean, that you
don't want to have

00:09:17.623 --> 00:09:18.991
a transition meeting with Biden,

00:09:18.991 --> 00:09:20.493
but can you at least
give him a heads up

00:09:20.493 --> 00:09:21.927
that he should get
a different ride?

00:09:21.927 --> 00:09:23.996
[ As Trump ]
Yeah, in regards to the limo,

00:09:23.996 --> 00:09:25.965
it might be easier just
to replace it.

00:09:25.965 --> 00:09:29.502
Anyway, the claim Trump's teams
have been making are so insane,

00:09:29.502 --> 00:09:31.036
most lawyers want no part of it.

00:09:31.036 --> 00:09:32.037
The Trump team even tried

00:09:32.037 --> 00:09:33.606
to delay a hearing
in federal court,

00:09:33.606 --> 00:09:35.774
but as a reporter
for Reuters noted,

00:09:35.774 --> 00:09:37.076
the judge wasn't having it...

00:09:51.223 --> 00:09:53.325
I mean, every word
of that Tweet is perfect.

00:09:53.325 --> 00:09:56.562
He wants to overturn the results
of a state he lost,

00:09:56.562 --> 00:09:59.498
but his lawyers quit,
so he's using a radio host,

00:09:59.498 --> 00:10:01.300
and the judge actually needed

00:10:01.300 --> 00:10:03.035
to tell the radio host
to be prepared.

00:10:03.035 --> 00:10:04.203
"Of course I'm prepared.

00:10:04.203 --> 00:10:05.671
I brought my soundboard,
Your Honor.

00:10:05.671 --> 00:10:08.407
This was a fraud to a degree
that we should all be alarmed!"

00:10:08.407 --> 00:10:11.677
[ Laughter ]
[ Vuvuzela blasting ]

00:10:11.677 --> 00:10:12.878
"I rest my case."

00:10:12.878 --> 00:10:15.614
So, then, Trump put
Rudy Giuliani in charge

00:10:15.614 --> 00:10:17.916
and this will probably
not shock you --

00:10:17.916 --> 00:10:18.917
it didn't work out great.

00:10:18.917 --> 00:10:20.353
For example, yesterday,

00:10:20.353 --> 00:10:23.823
the Pennsylvania Supreme Court
ruled against the Trump campaign

00:10:23.823 --> 00:10:25.691
in yet another one
of their ridiculous lawsuits.

00:10:25.691 --> 00:10:27.860
Of course, Rudy never
made it to the hearing

00:10:27.860 --> 00:10:29.528
because he accidentally went

00:10:29.528 --> 00:10:31.797
to the Pennsylvania
Supreme Food Court

00:10:31.797 --> 00:10:33.132
at the King of Prussia Mall.

00:10:33.132 --> 00:10:34.900
[ As Giuliani ]
Your Honor, I object!

00:10:34.900 --> 00:10:38.637
"Alright. So do you want like
the chicken teriyaki, instead?"

00:10:38.637 --> 00:10:40.640
And then, yesterday,
reporters and court observers

00:10:40.640 --> 00:10:42.508
who were covering
a Trump campaign case

00:10:42.508 --> 00:10:44.810
in front of a federal judge
in Pennsylvania

00:10:44.810 --> 00:10:48.380
pulled out individual lines
from Rudy's oral arguments

00:10:48.380 --> 00:10:50.482
and they're just
a delight to read.

00:10:50.482 --> 00:10:51.751
I mean, here are a few examples

00:10:51.751 --> 00:10:55.120
of actual legal arguments
from Rudy Giuliani,

00:10:55.120 --> 00:10:56.856
you know, the guy who was
once -- and this is true --

00:10:56.856 --> 00:10:59.091
the mayor of New York City.

00:10:59.091 --> 00:11:01.193
one of our biggest cities,
the biggest...

00:11:11.837 --> 00:11:14.040
Incredible.
It's like watching a livestream

00:11:14.040 --> 00:11:15.874
of a wino doing
open heart surgery.

00:11:15.874 --> 00:11:17.943
"What the hell is this thing
and why is it moving?"

00:11:17.943 --> 00:11:19.077
That's the heart.

00:11:19.077 --> 00:11:20.846
"Oh.
Should we put it back in?"

00:11:20.846 --> 00:11:22.147
The term "strict scrutiny"

00:11:22.147 --> 00:11:24.883
is one of the most basic
legal concepts in all of law,

00:11:24.883 --> 00:11:27.786
but, then, if he knew
what strict scrutiny was,

00:11:27.786 --> 00:11:30.823
he'd have gotten his bottom
teeth capped as well.

00:11:30.823 --> 00:11:33.158
If your lawyer says they don't
know what strict scrutiny means,

00:11:33.158 --> 00:11:35.727
then it's, you know,
time to get someone new.

00:11:35.727 --> 00:11:37.796
I mean, that's like
if your lawyer got up in court

00:11:37.796 --> 00:11:39.732
and asked to cross-examine
a witness

00:11:39.732 --> 00:11:42.501
and then asked his questions
with his eyes like this --

00:11:42.501 --> 00:11:43.635
[ Laughing ]

00:11:43.635 --> 00:11:45.905
This was, by far,
the best exchange

00:11:45.905 --> 00:11:47.406
and summed up the stupidity

00:11:47.406 --> 00:11:49.141
of this moronic
little coup attempt

00:11:49.141 --> 00:11:50.509
as much as any moment could.

00:11:57.716 --> 00:11:59.718
I would love to see Rudy
at a spelling bee.

00:11:59.718 --> 00:12:01.720
The word is opacity.

00:12:01.720 --> 00:12:04.590
[ Giuliani ]
Can you use it incorrectly
in a sentence, please?

00:12:04.590 --> 00:12:06.591
Oh, Rudy, sweet Rudy,
I won't miss Trump,

00:12:06.591 --> 00:12:08.260
but I also won't miss you.

00:12:08.260 --> 00:12:09.494
I hope, when this is over,

00:12:09.494 --> 00:12:11.931
you take a well-earned trip
to the Bahamas.

00:12:11.931 --> 00:12:14.232
No, I meant the island.
Never mind.

00:12:14.232 --> 00:12:17.536
Rudy's deranged performance
was such an embarrassing debacle

00:12:17.536 --> 00:12:19.705
that even close Trump ally
Mick Mulvaney,

00:12:19.705 --> 00:12:21.140
Trump's former chief of staff

00:12:21.140 --> 00:12:24.009
and a guy who is fully onboard
with this grotesque attempt

00:12:24.009 --> 00:12:26.512
to overturn the results
of the election, said today...

00:12:30.415 --> 00:12:33.184
Yet, last night, after Rudy's
disastrous bungling

00:12:33.184 --> 00:12:34.619
of, you know, everything,

00:12:34.619 --> 00:12:37.288
here's what Fox News host
Sean Hannity told his audience

00:12:37.288 --> 00:12:38.523 line:0%
about Rudy's performance.

00:12:38.523 --> 00:12:40.059 line:0%
-In Pennsylvania,

00:12:40.059 --> 00:12:42.327 line:0%
Rudy Giuliani
argued the case today.

00:12:42.327 --> 00:12:44.229 line:0%
I've heard from more
than a few people

00:12:44.229 --> 00:12:48.200 line:0%
that he was absolutely brilliant
in his arguments today.

00:12:48.200 --> 00:12:50.669
-Maybe he was saying it the way
British people use "brilliant,"

00:12:50.669 --> 00:12:51.937
to mean "funny."

00:12:51.937 --> 00:12:53.205
[ English accent ]
Did you see Mr. Bean fall

00:12:53.205 --> 00:12:55.674
down that escalator
into the savory pie display?

00:12:55.674 --> 00:12:57.809
Brilliant!
Absolutely brilliant.

00:12:57.809 --> 00:13:00.513
Fun fact -- the original title
of Hannity's show was...

00:13:03.782 --> 00:13:06.118
We're in the midst of several
crises colliding at once --

00:13:06.118 --> 00:13:07.952
the destruction
of American democracy,

00:13:07.952 --> 00:13:09.254
a deadly plague

00:13:09.254 --> 00:13:12.357
that killed 1,500 Americans
just yesterday alone,

00:13:12.357 --> 00:13:13.992
and we're seeing, once again,
that the Republican Party

00:13:13.992 --> 00:13:15.961
simply does not care
about either.

00:13:15.961 --> 00:13:17.162
It's an authoritarian movement

00:13:17.162 --> 00:13:18.563
willing to wreck
the American system

00:13:18.563 --> 00:13:20.732
and stand idly by
while Americans die.

00:13:20.732 --> 00:13:23.669
Even after Trump leaves office,
what we're seeing now is

00:13:23.669 --> 00:13:25.904
that Trumpism
will very much remain.

00:13:25.904 --> 00:13:27.072
At least we can be sure that,

00:13:27.072 --> 00:13:28.974
what we here at "Late Night"
are calling...

00:13:30.543 --> 00:13:33.412 line:0%
will almost certainly fail
and, for now, there won't be...

00:13:33.412 --> 00:13:35.280 line:0%
-A second Trump
administration.

